  <title>Documents</title>

  <p><guiseq><gui>General</gui><gui>Create document</gui></guiseq> makes a
  document for a customer, of one of the types set up in <link
  xref="settings#document_types">the settings</link>. A posted document waits
  in <link xref="documents_to_invoice"/> until its products are invoiced.
  Lines are saved as you type them.</p>

  <steps>
    <item><p>Choose the document type in the box beside <gui>Document
    types</gui>. The window and its post button take its name. <gui>Document
    types</gui> opens the settings to add one.</p></item>
    <item><p>Choose the customer. <gui>Customer</gui> opens the contacts
    window.</p></item>
    <item><p>Click <gui>New document</gui>, or <gui>Existing documents</gui>
    to carry on with one of this customer's unposted documents of this
    type. The button shows how many there are.</p></item>
    <item><p>Click <gui>New Item</gui>, or press <key>F2</key>, for each line,
    and fill in the <gui>Qty</gui> and <gui>Product</gui>. The <gui>Qty</gui>
    can be a sum such as <input>2x12</input>; see
    <link xref="qty_arithmetic"/>. Choosing the product
    fills in the customer's <gui>Price</gui> for it, which you can change.
    <gui>Delete Item</gui>, or <key>F3</key>, removes the selected line.</p>
    <p>You can also scan or type a barcode into <gui>Scan or Type in +
    Enter</gui>, or drag a product onto the list from <link xref="products"/>
    or <link xref="product_search"/>. A product already on the document adds
    to its line's <gui>Qty</gui>; any other gets a new line at the customer's
    price. A barcode no product has is reported.</p></item>
    <item><p>Check the date and <gui>Comments</gui>, and click the post
    button.</p></item>
  </steps>

  <p><gui>Minimum</gui>, <gui>Maximum</gui>, <gui>Retailer</gui>,
  <gui>Freeze</gui>, <gui>Priority</gui> and <gui>S Price</gui> are extra
  fields that print on the document, for document types whose template uses
  them. Right click a line and choose <gui>Set retailer to None</gui> to clear
  its retailer. Which columns are shown is set in <link
  xref="settings#columns">the settings</link>.</p>

  <p>To change your mind when posting, check <gui>Cancel printing and
  posting</gui> on the <gui>PyGtk Posting</gui> tab of the print dialog, then
  click <gui>Print</gui>. Nothing is printed or posted, and the document stays
  open. Closing the print dialog with <gui>Cancel</gui> instead still posts the
  document, without printing it. Use <gui>View document</gui> to check it
  first.</p>

  <p><gui>Delete document</gui> asks first, then deletes the current document
  and all its lines.</p>

  <section id="menu">
  <title>The window menu</title>
  <terms>
    <item><title><gui>Cancel</gui></title>
    <p>Closes the window. The document stays unposted.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Email invoice</gui></title>
    <p>When checked, posting also opens <link xref="send_email"/> to the
    customer with the document attached. If they have no email address, a
    message says the document was posted but not emailed.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Import items from history</gui></title>
    <p>Opens <link xref="document_history"/>; choose a past document and
    click <gui>Import items from document history</gui> to copy its lines
    into this one.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Print without confirming</gui></title>
    <p>Prints straight to the printer when posting, with no print
    dialog.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>View document</gui></title>
    <p>Shows the document as it will print.</p></item>
  </terms>
  </section>

</page>
